{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gBX8WApwFJKqCNMvbQ1Wd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-claude-sandboxed-profile\n3\tstatus: in-progress\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-09\n5\tcompleted_at:\n6\tsupersedes:\n7\tdepends_on:\n8\tremediates:\n9\tpriority: 1\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: feature\n12\tdelivers: capability:claude-sandboxed-profile\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t# Spec: The Claude agent offers a sandboxed access profile\n16\t\n17\t## 1. Intent\n18\t\n19\t### Goal\n20\t\n21\tA task handed to Claude can run with write access inside an operating-system sandbox, as one handed to Codex can, and the profile refuses to start, naming how to install what is missing, when the sandbox cannot be enforced.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\t\n25\tCodex has two command profiles, `read` and `sandboxed` (`-s workspace-write`), restricted by the operating system. Claude had only `read`, restricted by the agent's own permission list, which cannot exclude a flag that writes a file or runs a program; that is why its reviewer profile had to give up `go test`. Claude Code has a sandbox of its own (`sandbox.enabled`, on bubblewrap and socat) that a profile can switch on with `--settings`. Without socat it prints a warning and runs the commands unsandboxed, so enabling it blindly would claim a guarantee that is not enforced.\n26\t\n27\t### Constraints\n28\t\n29\t- The mechanism is the delegation policy: a `sandboxed` command and its resumed form on the agent. No engine change, no new field.\n30\t- The check of the dependencies lives in the profile's own command, so it runs wherever the profile runs.\n31\t\n32\t### Non-goals\n33\t\n34\t- Giving the reviews write access: a review accepts only `read`.\n35\t- Changing the `read` profile.\n36\t\n37\t## 2. Requirements\n38\t\n39\t### Functional\n40\t\n41\t- R1: The `claude-opus-5-5` agent shall declare a `sandboxed` command, and the same for its resumed run, that turns on the Claude Code sandbox with unsandboxed commands disallowed.\n42\t- R2: Before it starts Claude, that command shall check for `bwrap` and `socat` (not on macOS, whose sandbox has no such dependency) and, when one is missing, write to stderr which one, why it matters and the install command for Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora and Arch, and exit 127 without starting Claude.\n43\t- R4: A profile may declare `requires` (executables, operating systems that skip them, an install hint); `pose delegate agents` shall list a profile whose executables are missing as `unavailable_access=<profile>(missing …; install: …)` and `pose doctor` shall warn (`delegation.requirements`) with the same hint, before the profile is used. The block is not part of the adapter a run binds.\n44\t- R3: With the dependencies present, a task with `--access sandboxed` shall write inside its working directory and be refused a write outside it by the operating system.\n45\t\n46\t### Non-functional\n47\t\n48\t- The check adds no process beyond `sh`; it costs a `command -v` per dependency.\n49\t\n50\t### Security\n51\t\n52\t- The profile enforces nothing it cannot enforce: it does not start without the sandbox, rather than starting without it.\n53\t\n54\t### Compatibility\n55\t\n56\t- `read` access and the review profiles are unchanged. Codex is unchanged.\n57\t\n58\t## 3. Technical Plan\n59\t\n60\t### Affected areas\n61\t\n62\t`.pose/policy/delegation.json` of this repository and, by the same block, of instances that adopt it.\n63\t\n64\t### Artifacts\n65\t\n66\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.md\n67\t- created: .pose/starts/pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.json\n68\t- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.md\n69\t- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n70\t- modified: .pose/policy/delegation.json\n71\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_profile_test.go\n72\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_policy.go\n73\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n74\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n75\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_requirements_test.go\n76\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/engine_reads_raw_history_test.go\n77\t\n78\t### Delivery targets\n79\t\n80\t- capability:claude-sandboxed-profile module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n81\t\n82\t### API/contract changes\n83\t\n84\t`pose delegate agents` lists `access=read,sandboxed` for Claude and `unavailable_access=` for a profile whose executables are missing (JSON: `unavailable_access`); the policy gains an optional `requires` per agent; `delegate task --access sandboxed --agent claude-opus-5-5` is accepted.\n85\t\n86\t## 4. Tasks\n87\t\n88\t- [x] Measure the Claude Code sandbox (bwrap present, socat missing, then installed)\n89\t- [x] Declare the profile with the dependency check in front of Claude\n90\t- [x] Run a sandboxed task: a write inside succeeds, a write outside is refused by the operating system\n91\t- [x] Test the check with the dependencies absent\n92\t- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n93\t\n94\t## 5. Decisions\n95\t\n96\t### Decision D1\n97\t- Basis: R2\n98\t- Minimal option: enable the sandbox in settings and rely on Claude Code's warning\n99\t- Selected option: a check in the command that refuses to start\n100\t- Rationale: with socat missing Claude Code only warns and runs unsandboxed, so a task handed over as sandboxed would run with the access of an unsandboxed one\n101\t- Consequences: the profile needs `sh`; a machine without the dependencies fails the task at once with the install hint\n102\t- Falsifier: a sandboxed task that starts Claude without the sandbox in force\n103\t\n104\t## 6. Validation\n105\t\n106\t### Strategy\n107\t\n108\tThe command's check is run with an empty PATH and must stop with 127 and the hint; a task was run on this machine after socat was installed and wrote inside its directory and was refused outside.\n109\t\n110\t### Deterministic checks\n111\t\n112\t`go test` of the tests named in the trace; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n113\t\n114\t### Requirement trace\n115\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestTheClaudeAgentDeclaresASandboxedProfileThatTurnsTheSandboxOn check:claude-sandboxed-profile-integration\n116\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheSandboxedProfileRefusesToStartWithoutItsDependenciesAndSaysHowToInstallThem\n117\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestTheSandboxedProfileStartsWhenTheDependenciesArePresent\n118\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestTheDelegationPolicyReportsTheMissingRequirementsOfAProfile test:TestDelegateAgentsAndDoctorSayHowToInstallWhatAProfileNeeds\n119\t\n120\t### Known gaps\n121\t- The doctor warning is covered by the shared `MissingRequirements` test and the `delegate agents` output test, not by its own doctor test.\n122\t- R3 was exercised by hand on this machine (a write inside the working directory succeeded, a write to the home directory was refused with \"read-only file system\"); the automated tests cover the declaration and the dependency check, not the operating-system refusal, which needs Claude and bubblewrap.\n123\t- Instances other than this repository adopt the profile by copying the block into their own `delegation.json`.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## 7. Final Report\n128\t\n129\t### Delivered scope\n130\tThe Claude agent declares `sandboxed` (and its resumed form) with the Claude Code sandbox on and unsandboxed commands off, behind a check that refuses to start, with the install command, when bubblewrap or socat is missing (R1, R2); a sandboxed task writes inside its directory and is refused outside by the operating system (R3). Left out: write access for reviews.\n131\t\n132\t### Files and modules changed\n133\t- .pose/policy/delegation.json (the Claude agent), pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_profile_test.go\n134\t- the validation matrix gains `claude-sandboxed-profile-integration`\n135\t\n136\t### Validation executed\n137\t- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n138\t- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n139\t\n140\t### Residual risks\n141\t- The sandbox is Claude Code's, on bubblewrap or seatbelt: its limits are theirs.\n142\t- On a platform whose sandbox needs other dependencies than bwrap and socat the check is wrong until updated.\n143\t\n144\t### Follow-ups\n145\t\n146\t- [open] Let the reviewer profile of Claude use the sandbox to allow `go test` again, (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n147\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f5fccead-2e1a-45bf-bed7-9cdb0f22cd4e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T20:47:29.035Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3567912673/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-claude-sandboxed-profile\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-09\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on:\nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\ndelivers: capability:claude-sandboxed-profile\n---\n\n# Spec: The Claude agent offers a sandboxed access profile\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\n\nA task handed to Claude can run with write access inside an operating-system sandbox, as one handed to Codex can, and the profile refuses to start, naming how to install what is missing, when the sandbox cannot be enforced.\n\n### Business value\n\nCodex has two command profiles, `read` and `sandboxed` (`-s workspace-write`), restricted by the operating system. Claude had only `read`, restricted by the agent's own permission list, which cannot exclude a flag that writes a file or runs a program; that is why its reviewer profile had to give up `go test`. Claude Code has a sandbox of its own (`sandbox.enabled`, on bubblewrap and socat) that a profile can switch on with `--settings`. Without socat it prints a warning and runs the commands unsandboxed, so enabling it blindly would claim a guarantee that is not enforced.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- The mechanism is the delegation policy: a `sandboxed` command and its resumed form on the agent. No engine change, no new field.\n- The check of the dependencies lives in the profile's own command, so it runs wherever the profile runs.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Giving the reviews write access: a review accepts only `read`.\n- Changing the `read` profile.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n- R1: The `claude-opus-5-5` agent shall declare a `sandboxed` command, and the same for its resumed run, that turns on the Claude Code sandbox with unsandboxed commands disallowed.\n- R2: Before it starts Claude, that command shall check for `bwrap` and `socat` (not on macOS, whose sandbox has no such dependency) and, when one is missing, write to stderr which one, why it matters and the install command for Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora and Arch, and exit 127 without starting Claude.\n- R4: A profile may declare `requires` (executables, operating systems that skip them, an install hint); `pose delegate agents` shall list a profile whose executables are missing as `unavailable_access=<profile>(missing …; install: …)` and `pose doctor` shall warn (`delegation.requirements`) with the same hint, before the profile is used. The block is not part of the adapter a run binds.\n- R3: With the dependencies present, a task with `--access sandboxed` shall write inside its working directory and be refused a write outside it by the operating system.\n\n### Non-functional\n\n- The check adds no process beyond `sh`; it costs a `command -v` per dependency.\n\n### Security\n\n- The profile enforces nothing it cannot enforce: it does not start without the sandbox, rather than starting without it.\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- `read` access and the review profiles are unchanged. Codex is unchanged.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n\n`.pose/policy/delegation.json` of this repository and, by the same block, of instances that adopt it.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.md\n- created: .pose/starts/pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.json\n- created: .pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-claude-sandboxed-profile.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n- modified: .pose/policy/delegation.json\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_profile_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_policy.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_requirements_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/engine_reads_raw_history_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:claude-sandboxed-profile module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\n### API/contract changes\n\n`pose delegate agents` lists `access=read,sandboxed` for Claude and `unavailable_access=` for a profile whose executables are missing (JSON: `unavailable_access`); the policy gains an optional `requires` per agent; `delegate task --access sandboxed --agent claude-opus-5-5` is accepted.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n- [x] Measure the Claude Code sandbox (bwrap present, socat missing, then installed)\n- [x] Declare the profile with the dependency check in front of Claude\n- [x] Run a sandboxed task: a write inside succeeds, a write outside is refused by the operating system\n- [x] Test the check with the dependencies absent\n- [ ] Independent review and closeout\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R2\n- Minimal option: enable the sandbox in settings and rely on Claude Code's warning\n- Selected option: a check in the command that refuses to start\n- Rationale: with socat missing Claude Code only warns and runs unsandboxed, so a task handed over as sandboxed would run with the access of an unsandboxed one\n- Consequences: the profile needs `sh`; a machine without the dependencies fails the task at once with the install hint\n- Falsifier: a sandboxed task that starts Claude without the sandbox in force\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\n\nThe command's check is run with an empty PATH and must stop with 127 and the hint; a task was run on this machine after socat was installed and wrote inside its directory and was refused outside.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n`go test` of the tests named in the trace; the strict matrix in a clean clone.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestTheClaudeAgentDeclaresASandboxedProfileThatTurnsTheSandboxOn check:claude-sandboxed-profile-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheSandboxedProfileRefusesToStartWithoutItsDependenciesAndSaysHowToInstallThem\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestTheSandboxedProfileStartsWhenTheDependenciesArePresent\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestTheDelegationPolicyReportsTheMissingRequirementsOfAProfile test:TestDelegateAgentsAndDoctorSayHowToInstallWhatAProfileNeeds\n\n### Known gaps\n- The doctor warning is covered by the shared `MissingRequirements` test and the `delegate agents` output test, not by its own doctor test.\n- R3 was exercised by hand on this machine (a write inside the working directory succeeded, a write to the home directory was refused with \"read-only file system\"); the automated tests cover the declaration and the dependency check, not the operating-system refusal, which needs Claude and bubblewrap.\n- Instances other than this repository adopt the profile by copying the block into their own `delegation.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe Claude agent declares `sandboxed` (and its resumed form) with the Claude Code sandbox on and unsandboxed commands off, behind a check that refuses to start, with the install command, when bubblewrap or socat is missing (R1, R2); a sandboxed task writes inside its directory and is refused outside by the operating system (R3). Left out: write access for reviews.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- .pose/policy/delegation.json (the Claude agent), pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_profile_test.go\n- the validation matrix gains `claude-sandboxed-profile-integration`\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` on a clean clone of the reviewed head\n- Result: recorded by the sealed validation evidence; independent delegated review concluded with `pose review conclude`.\n\n### Residual risks\n- The sandbox is Claude Code's, on bubblewrap or seatbelt: its limits are theirs.\n- On a platform whose sandbox needs other dependencies than bwrap and socat the check is wrong until updated.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] Let the reviewer profile of Claude use the sandbox to allow `go test` again, (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-01-08)\n","numLines":147,"startLine":1,"totalLines":147}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017gBX8WApwFJKqCNMvbQ1Wd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
